{{also|défiance|Defiance}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} ''[[défiance|defiance]]'', from ''[[défiant]]'' (present participle of ''[[défier]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/dɪˈfaɪ(j)əns/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-defiance.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪəns|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The feeling, or spirit of being [[defiant]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author={{w|Ben Travers}}
|chapter=6|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1521052W A Cuckoo in the Nest]
|passage=But Sophia's mother was not the woman to brook '''defiance'''. After a few moments' vain remonstrance her husband complied. His manner and appearance were suggestive of a satiated sea-lion.}}
# Open or bold [[resistance]] to or [[disregard]] for [[authority]], [[opposition]], or [[power]].
# A challenging attitude or behaviour; [[challenge]].

